      "description": "Text to video on OliviaRossi's PRISM-PIKA, a merge of Singularity v2 and 10Eros Max with Pika H3 Flex built in at 0.85, so there is no adapter to load. A five-second shot takes about 60 seconds at 480p and about 2 3/4 minutes at 768p on a 12 GB card.\n\nIt looks close to Pika Flex with stronger light. A locked-off prompt held still, a quiet-room prompt stayed quiet, and sound levels matched stock H3. Fast motion can blur heavily: on a motorbike test the wall behind the rider smeared.\n\nIt runs Pika Flex's six-step schedule. The author gives no settings, so that choice is ours. There is no step control.\n\nWrite the prompt the H3 way: style, then each shot with its camera move, then sound. Give each camera move an end point.\n\nDo not add a turbo or speed LoRA in the LoRA slot. Pika warn that a second accelerator breaks the output, and this checkpoint has Pika built in.\n\nThe author says the licence follows the source models (Singularity v2, 10Eros Max, Pika H3 Flex), so check them before use, along with the territorial and commercial-use terms of the MiniMax H3 Community License.",
