      "description": "Reference to video on OliviaRossi's PRISM-PIKA, a merge of Singularity v2 and 10Eros Max with Pika H3 Flex built in at 0.85, so there is no adapter to load. A five-second 480p shot with two pictures takes about 70 seconds on a 12 GB card.\n\nThe pictures never appear in the video, so the prompt must describe the whole shot. Name each picture as <Picture 1>, <Picture 2> and so on, as in H3's full reference format. Give each camera move an end point.\n\nOn Pika's sample it kept a pilot's helmet with its visor lights and a saucer-shaped space station from one picture each, on all three seeds. The station's hull came out cleaner and simpler than the picture. Reference clips and sounds are wired but were not tested.\n\nIt runs Pika Flex's six-step schedule. The author gives no settings, so that choice is ours. There is no step control.\n\nDo not add a turbo or speed LoRA in the LoRA slot. Pika warn that a second accelerator breaks the output, and this checkpoint has Pika built in.\n\nThe author says the licence follows the source models (Singularity v2, 10Eros Max, Pika H3 Flex), so check them before use, along with the territorial and commercial-use terms of the MiniMax H3 Community License.",
